Pin an LCSC id on EVERY part. Prefer Basic tier; justify every Extended part.
For each part, the "value" field must describe the pinned LCSC part itself,
not the value the circuit wanted. If they differ, say so in "mismatch".

For polarised or multi-pin parts (diodes, LEDs, MOSFETs, ICs, sensors) give
the pin-1 / polarity marking and which net each pin lands on. This is where a
reversed flyback diode shorts 12 V to ground.

